# ClearMark API — environment
# Copy to .env (or set in your shell / Docker) and fill in what you use.
# Everything here is OPTIONAL: with nothing set, the API runs the local CPU
# pipeline (LaMa full-res tiling) exactly like v1.1.

# --- Local inpaint device -------------------------------------------------
# auto (default: use CUDA if available) | cpu | cuda
LAMA_DEVICE=auto

# --- PRO tier: local SDXL diffusion inpainting (hard cases) ----------------
# Off by default. Set to 1 to enable the "PRO" mode on the remove page — first
# use downloads ~7 GB and needs an 8 GB+ GPU (crop + CPU-offload fit RTX 3060 Ti).
# SDXL_ENABLE=1

# --- Optional: SAM 2 / SAM mask refinement (tighter edges) -----------------
# Off by default. Needs SAM installed + a checkpoint:
#   pip install "git+https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2.git"   (SAM 2), OR
#   pip install segment-anything  + set SAM_CHECKPOINT=<path to sam .pth>
# SAM_ENABLE=1
# SAM_CHECKPOINT=C:\models\sam_vit_b.pth
# SAM_MODEL_TYPE=vit_b

# --- GPU serverless worker (Phase 2) --------------------------------------
# When set, image detect/erase and all video jobs route to the worker
# (Florence-2 + SAM2 detect, LaMa/SDXL erase, Real-ESRGAN, ProPainter video).
# Unreachable worker → automatic fallback to local CPU for images.
# GPU_WORKER_URL=https://<you>--clearmark-worker-web.modal.run
# GPU_WORKER_TOKEN=change-me-to-a-long-random-secret
# GPU_WORKER_TIMEOUT=180
# VIDEO_TIMEOUT=1800
# Removal model routing on the worker: 3.0 = LaMa (fast/cheap), 4.0 = SDXL (hard).
# GPU_PREDICT_MODE=3.0

# --- Video storage (Phase 2) ----------------------------------------------
# Unset → clips are kept in the OS temp dir with a 1-hour TTL (fine for one box).
# Set these to use Cloudflare R2 (S3 API) so results survive and scale.
# R2_ENDPOINT=https://<accountid>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
# R2_BUCKET=clearmark
# R2_ACCESS_KEY=...
# R2_SECRET_KEY=...
# R2_PUBLIC_BASE=https://media.example.com   # optional public read host
